<h2>Where percentage deductibles show up in Utah</h2>
<p>Earthquake endorsements almost always use a percentage deductible, often 10% to 20% of the dwelling limit. Some Utah policies also use a percentage deductible for wind or hail. Your declarations page lists each deductible and how it’s calculated.</p>
<h2>How it affects a dispute</h2>
<p>The deductible doesn’t change the amount of loss an appraisal panel decides. It changes what you receive. If the loss sits near the deductible, a disputed amount may not be worth the cost of appraisal. If the loss is well above it, every additional dollar of the award reaches you.</p>
<h2>An illustrative example</h2>
<p>With the default figures, a 10% deductible on a $520,000 dwelling limit is $52,000. A $46,000 loss falls entirely within it, so no payment would be owed under that deductible, while the same loss under a $1,000 flat deductible would pay $45,000.</p>
<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does the percentage apply to contents?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>The percentage is usually calculated from the dwelling limit and applied to the whole loss under that peril. Wording varies, so check your endorsement.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I lower my earthquake deductible?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Options depend on the carrier. Lower deductibles generally cost more. Ask your agent at renewal.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free calculators</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/utah-claim-calculators/claim-timeline-planner/"><small>Planner</small><span>Claim Timeline Planner</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-claim-calculators/appraisal-readiness-checkup/"><small>Checklist</small><span>Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-claim-calculators/roof-snow-load-estimator/"><small>Estimator</small><span>Roof Snow Load Estimator</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-t">Talk it through, free</h2><p>Send the carrier’s estimate or call. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal is worth it.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+184